# The pinned Firefox ESR for Phase 1 (P1.6.4, issue #36).
#
# Shell-sourceable on purpose: fetch-esr.sh reads it, CI reads it, and a human
# reads it. There is exactly one place the version lives.
#
# WHY A MOZILLA TARBALL RATHER THAN A DISTRO PACKAGE.
#
#   1. Arch ships no firefox-esr at all, so on the development machine there
#      is no packaged ESR to pin to in the first place.
#   2. Even where one exists (Debian's firefox-esr, Ubuntu's snap), the
#      version is the distro's to move. "Pin an ESR so the target stops
#      moving" (R4) is not satisfied by a name that resolves to a different
#      build next month, and Firefox's Wayland path changes between releases
#      -- which is the entire reason R4 exists.
#   3. The tarball is version-exact and content-addressed: the checksum below
#      is Mozilla's own published SHA256SUMS entry for this file, so the pin
#      is verifiable rather than merely stated. A pin that is not checksummed
#      is not a pin.
#
# UPGRADING IS A DELIBERATE ACT (the issue says so: "upgrade deliberately, not
# by drift"). To move to a new ESR: change the three values below, re-run
# fetch-esr.sh, re-run the acceptance script, and REGENERATE the checked-in
# globals ledger (shim/docs/globals-touched-firefox-140.12.0esr.log) -- a new
# Firefox may want different globals, and that file is the evidence the v0
# global set is argued from.

VITRIN_FIREFOX_VERSION=140.12.0esr
VITRIN_FIREFOX_SHA256=3323ee13ac6fe4877fa2e1f4a3aa6b8009f65a620c7bbca96fe86f1a6f433d92
VITRIN_FIREFOX_URL=https://download-installer.cdn.mozilla.net/pub/firefox/releases/140.12.0esr/linux-x86_64/en-US/firefox-140.12.0esr.tar.xz

# Where fetch-esr.sh unpacks it. Gitignored (see the repo root .gitignore):
# neither the tarball nor the unpacked browser is ever committed.
VITRIN_FIREFOX_DIR=shim/.firefox
